ar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"756342c343a00f743ef9b299d90ae1ab627fa30c8d129aa32a5761509609e699","event_uuid":"e3f19315-96ec-479d-8df1-f07f124c8324","position":{"commit_sha":"a715f417317ee38d6e07fcc936f2f21457776ce1","position":"1795041092365390118-e3f19315-96ec-479d-8df1-f07f124c8324"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"9960747a3ff66c1b932f9a69c85093883a107ffec3cc8f9e7626d5153f1e0681","event_uuid":"7293866a-9030-4ef4-bddf-58416506a5a5","position":{"commit_sha":"8ab65b560da25dc1d63e4c08c9aaeeee1c6b29e6","position":"1795041100396843639-7293866a-9030-4ef4-bddf-58416506a5a5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Occurrence 2026-11-04 ~09:50 PST: a CLI close (rebar transition smalltime-repressive-sealion in_progress closed --class preexisting, worktree fix-sealion) left pid 61352 at PPID 1 running rebar._commands.compact_trigger.run_detached_sweep on the main tracker. It was left to finish rather than killed mid-compaction; it exited on its own within about 1 minute, and scripts/check_orphaned_load.py then exited 0.","timestamp":1793815198196924001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3426 merged to main as 9d205edbd45fc9aad76538f5e6e9a19ab5f5200e (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments). All 6 acceptance criteria checked against origin/main: AGENTS.md's PPID 1 bullet names compact_trigger, gc_trigger and _store.push; docs/orphaned-processes.md names all 3, says to leave them, calls the sweep safe to interrupt and prefers SIGTERM; scripts/check_orphaned_load.py has is_rebar_detached_worker and the \"rebar detached worker\" report label; tests/unit/test_orphaned_processes_guidance.py has test_guidance_names_every_spawn_detached_worker.\n\nWindows sweep: not needed. The change touches only guidance text, a pure string matcher over `ps` command-line text, and tests that inject records and spawn no process. It adds no subprocess, fd, path, encoding or permission handling, so it has nothing Windows-specific to break. (A Windows sweep is being dispatched anyway for the A1 stack after it lands; its result will cover main at that point.)","timestamp":1795040596611931876}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793763468882069001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8e578cc1-609d-4466-a735-bae26bd4bbb0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6cad-3200-050f-46cc"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAGENTS.md's mandatory rule says \"No process you start may reach PPID 1\", with no carve-out. rebar itself deliberately detaches three workers through `rebar._proc.spawn_detached` (`start_new_session=True` on POSIX, `DETACHED_PROCESS` on Windows) so a CLI command can return while they finish: the compaction sweep (`rebar._commands.compact_trigger.run_detached_sweep`), snapshot GC (`rebar._snapshot.gc_trigger.run_detached`) and the async tickets-branch push (`rebar._store.push.push_tickets_branch`). On 2026-11-03 two sessions (westbound-chivalric-pinemarten, overweak-deviant-shelduck) found a sweep at PPID 1 and believed they could not comply without killing rebar's own worker; on 2026-11-04 a CLI close left pid 61352 at PPID 1 running `run_detached_sweep`, which exited on its own within about a minute. `docs/orphaned-processes.md` says PPID 1 is a signal, not proof, but names none of rebar's workers, and `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` does not recognise them.\n\n## Decision: the guidance is wrong, not the code\nThe detach is deliberate design (each spawn site documents why the worker must outlive its command, and `spawn_detached` anchors a durable cwd for exactly that lifetime). The PPID 1 rule's own rationale is agent-started helpers (the 2026-08-22 busy-loop incident). These workers end on their own: the async push and GC are one-shot, and the sweep stops at its next ticket boundary on SIGTERM (`compact_trigger.install_stop_on_sigterm`). Making the CLI wait for them would change product behaviour, so the fix is a carve-out in the guidance plus recognition in the detector. No change to rebar's spawning code.\n\n## Approach\n1. AGENTS.md: amend the existing \"No process you start may reach PPID 1\" bullet in place with one sentence: processes rebar itself detaches (not ones the agent starts) are exempt; recognise them by a command line containing `import rebar._commands.compact_trigger`, `rebar._snapshot.gc_trigger` or `rebar._store.push`; leave them to finish; details in docs/orphaned-processes.md. No new section.\n2. docs/orphaned-processes.md: add a short \"rebar's own detached workers\" passage naming the three entry points and how to identify each from `ps -o pid=,ppid=,command=`. It must agree with rebar's existing runtime remedy in `src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py` (`_INTERRUPTIBLE_REMEDIES['compact-sweep']`: the sweep is optional housekeeping and safe to interrupt, losing no data because the events stay live and the next trigger re-folds them). So the guidance is: leave these workers alone because they exit on their own; if a sweep must be stopped (for example a blocked writer's LockTimeout names it), SIGTERM is preferred because it ends the sweep at a ticket boundary, and interrupting it loses no data.\n3. scripts/check_orphaned_load.py: add `is_rebar_detached_worker(command)` matching the `spawn_detached` command shape (`import <module>; <module>.<func>(`) for those three modules. When a flagged record matches, its report line carries a \"rebar detached worker\" label and the \"exits on its own; SIGTERM if it must stop\" note. It is still reported when over the CPU threshold, because a runaway worker is a real problem. Read-only behaviour unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n- `AGENTS.md`\n- `docs/orphaned-processes.md`\n- `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py`\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_orphaned_processes_guidance.py`\n\n## Testing\n- Detector: a record carrying the real `spawn_detached` command line for each of the three entry points is recognised. An unrelated `python -c 'while True: pass'` is not, and neither is a command that merely mentions `rebar` in an argument. A recognised record over the threshold is still flagged, and its report line carries the rebar-worker label.\n- Guidance: AGENTS.md and docs/orphaned-processes.md both name all three entry points. The test pins them against the module paths passed to `spawn_detached` in src/rebar, so a new spawn site without guidance fails it. A second test asserts the doc does not call the compaction sweep unsafe to interrupt, keeping it consistent with `lock_owner._INTERRUPTIBLE_REMEDIES`.\n- Portability: string matching on `ps` output only; tests inject records and never spawn processes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] AGENTS.md and docs/orphaned-processes.md agree that rebar's own detached workers (every `spawn_detached` caller: compaction sweep, snapshot GC, async push) are exempt from the PPID 1 rule.\n- [x] Both name how an agent identifies those workers by command line.\n- [x] docs/orphaned-processes.md tells agents to leave the workers to finish and, consistent with `lock_owner`'s compact-sweep remedy, that a sweep is safe to interrupt, with SIGTERM preferred if it must stop.\n- [x] scripts/check_orphaned_load.py recognises rebar's detached workers and labels them in its report, with tests in tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py.\n- [x] A test in tests/unit/test_orphaned_processes_guidance.py fails if a `spawn_detached` caller's module is not named in the guidance.\n- [x] `make verify` passes.\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"carve-out for rebar's own detached workers in the PPID 1 bullet"},{"path":"docs/orphaned-processes.md","reason":"name and identify rebar's detached workers"},{"path":"scripts/check_orphaned_load.py","reason":"recognise and label rebar detached workers"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py","reason":"detector recognition tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_orphaned_processes_guidance.py","reason":"guidance names every spawn_detached caller"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6cad-3200-050f-46cc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e3f19315-96ec-479d-8df1-f07f124c8324","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9d13-da09-73ec-491e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"AGENTS.md forbids PPID 1, but rebar detaches its own sweep","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["223f7ed0-e2bb-4ef0-a5be-f73e86d0f051","ea6ebc7b-80b5-4668-bbdd-32b2e3ea99ed","6b8f0220-7bde-4bc0-b634-2319f04dc880","e03afda6-98e8-4a3e-b927-fa68d42c9005","c6ea5048-716e-44a0-894a-a5963c6e681d","567bff22-f3f8-46ac-a7f8-d601fa400a67","84400692-6d96-4fe4-a84d-cc7ad05fb4c4","8e578cc1-609d-4466-a735-bae26bd4bbb0","43de811f-d81a-4d38-8150-06ed58e6918d","e76f9719-350e-4b6e-b756-6d8018ad056a","e29b8849-c49c-4c68-80b5-18919db99118","e3f19315-96ec-479d-8df1-f07f124c8324","7293866a-9030-4ef4-bddf-58416506a5a5"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795041100396843640,"uuid":"9561b2ae-72a1-48d7-829c-ab4dc3706a58"}
